{
"text": "Share by Email (opens in a new tab)",
"href": "mailto:?subject=Facebook&body=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2F902281863260413_1399580532329556+-+On+Saturday+night%2C+using+the+cover+of+darkness+and+masks%2C+about+a+dozen+men+stood+outside+Danbury+police+headquarters+holding+a+banner+that+read%2C+%E2%80%9CKeep+New+England+White.%E2%80%9DThis+racism+and+hate+cannot+go+unanswered.I+grew+up+in+Evanston%2C+Illinois%2C+a+community+much+like+Danbury+in+its+diversity.+In+our+neighboring+community+of+Skokie%2C+many+Holocaust+survivors+had+rebuilt+their+lives.+In+the+late+1970s%2C+neo-Nazis+sought+to+march+through+Skokie.+The+ensuing+legal+battle+ultimately+affirmed+their+First+Amendment+rights%2C+but+the+march+itself+never+took+place.+Instead%2C+the+threat+of+that+march+galvanized+Holocaust+survivors%2C+neighbors%2C+and+faith+leaders+to+stand+together+against+hatred+and+intimidation.That+important+lesson+has+stayed+with+me.Danbury%2C+and+every+city%2C+deserves+the+same+response.+We+cannot+answer+hatred+by+pretending+it+isn%27t+there%2C+and+we+cannot+answer+it+by+abandoning+the+principles+that+protect+everyone%27s+right+to+speak.+We+answer+it+by+standing+together+and+making+clear+that+intimidation+and+bigotry+do+not+represent+who+we+are.I+grew+up+in+a+community+committed+to+inclusion%2C+but+racism%2C+prejudice%2C+and+stereotyping+existed+there%2C+as+they+do+everywhere.+I+learned+early+that+this+is+a+fight+worth+fighting.+I%27ve+also+always+known+that+I+was+fortunate+to+be+born+in+this+country.+I+didn%E2%80%99t+earn+the+circumstances+of+my+birth%2C+and+I+don%27t+believe+anyone+should+be+judged%E2%80%94or+treated+as+more+or+less+American%E2%80%94because+of+where+they%2C+their+parents%2C+or+earlier+generations+were+born.Danbury+is+our+neighbor%2C+and+its+diversity+is+one+of+its+strengths.+It%E2%80%99s+part+of+what+makes+our+community%2C+our+region%2C+and+our+country+strong.We+must+never+be+silent+when+people+are+targeted+for+who+they+are+or+where+they+come+from.And%2C+we+must+not+let+a+handful+of+people+who+want+to+divide+us%2C+convince+us+that+they+speak+for+New+England.They+do+not.#antiracism #StandTogether #communityfirst #community #speakout"
},
{
"text": "Share by Email (opens in a new tab)",
